\subtree{
  \title{Decision}
  \p{In \code{VDC∞.{ℓ,s}}, \code{ℓ} measures the type of labels and \code{s} the simplex sets of presheaf values. A matrix ambient for \code{A : Type u} and entries in \code{Type v} uses labels \code{Type u : Type (u+1)} and matrix values in \code{Type (max u (v+1))}:}
  \p{\code{Mat(Set.{v};u) : VDC∞.{u+1, max u (v+1)}}.}
  \p{This is an intended elaboratable signature, to be tested in Lean. Its category projection still has \code{A : Type u} and \code{Hom : A → A → Type v}. The analogous spaces ambient has a classifier of small spaces in \code{sSet.{v+1}} and family collections at least \code{max u (v+1)}. Constructions involving all objects, monads, or diagrams explicitly compute any additional maxima or successors. No ban on necessary \code{max} expressions; \code{ULift} only raises universes. Yoneda's presheaf target and the allowable diagram sizes are stated explicitly and are not solved by augmentation.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rationale}
  \p{Entry size and collection size are different.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rejected}
  \p{The former \code{Mat.{u,v} : VDC∞.{u,v}} signature with labels \code{Type u}.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Acceptance}
  \p{\ref{at-fd-0001}, including \code{u<v}, \code{u=v}, \code{u>v}, and category-size examples.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Status}
  \p{minimal universe signatures compiled under AT-FD-1; semantic constructions remain provisional.}
}

\p{\em{Evidence update:} the minimal type contracts and generated universe table in \code{docs/foundations/} verify \ref{at-fd-0001}. The declaration uses explicit shape and proposition-valued-condition inputs; no root or interface is frozen by this size check.}
